
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
CA = CB [00]
A,C,D are collinear [01]
CE = CD [02]
C,B,E are collinear [03]
A,E,F are collinear [04]
F,B,D are collinear [05]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. CA = CB [00] & CE = CD [02] ⇒  CA:CB = CE:CD [06]
002. CA = CB [00] & CE = CD [02] ⇒  CA:CB = CD:CE [07]
003. C,D,A are collinear [01] & C,B,E are collinear [03] ⇒  ∠ACB = ∠DCE [08]
004. CA:CB = CE:CD [06] & ∠ACB = ∠DCE [08] (Similar Triangles)⇒  AC:EC = AB:ED [09]
005. CA:CB = CD:CE [07] & ∠ACB = ∠DCE [08] (Similar Triangles)⇒  ∠CAB = ∠CDE [10]
006. ∠CAB = ∠CDE [10] & A,C,D are collinear [01] ⇒  AB ∥ DE [11]
007. AB ∥ DE [11] & A,E,F are collinear [04] & F,B,D are collinear [05] ⇒  AF:FE = AB:ED [12]
008. AB ∥ DE [11] & A,E,F are collinear [04] & F,B,D are collinear [05] ⇒  AF:FE = FB:FD [13]
009. AC:EC = AB:ED [09] & CA = CB [00] & CE = CD [02] & AF:FE = AB:ED [12] & AF:FE = FB:FD [13] ⇒  FB:FD = CB:CD [14]
010. FB:FD = CB:CD [14] & F,B,D are collinear [05] ⇒  ∠BCF = ∠FCD [15]
011. ∠BCF = ∠FCD [15] & A,C,D are collinear [01] ⇒  ∠BCF = ∠FCA
==========================
